/-!
# Root geometry and Sylow fixers in even G₂

The genuine root predicates use the explicit long A-root and short C-root
maps of the octonion model. Central involutions in Sylow subgroups, both
in the full even model and in G₂(2)′, are proved long-root.

Subject only to the displayed automorphism-coverage hypotheses, every
pointwise Sylow fixer is inner, without an order restriction, and an
involutory fixer is induced by a long-root element. The binary argument
retains the full G₂(2) action on its proper commutator subgroup.

This establishes the model Sylow-fixer conclusions of Aschbacher–Smith
16.1.6, printed p.1172, under those coverage premises. Exhaustive root
conjugacy and the proper-parabolic centralizer and embedded two-residual
claims of 16.1.4(1), printed p.1171, remain separate obligations. No
central-cover lifting is claimed. See also the uses in 16.5.13–14,
printed pp.1201–1203, and LICENSES/ATLAS.txt for the root calculations.
-/
